<p>If your printer supports a toner saving function, this describes how 
 you can save on toner.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, this function may not be available.</p>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Quality:Standard</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="3">
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Toner Saving:</span> 
 list, select <span class="Term-Soft">On</span> or specify a toner saving 
 level.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Available items 
 might vary depending on your machine model.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="4">
<li><p>If you select <span class="Term-Soft">User Setting</span>, 
 click the <span class="Term-Soft">Toner Save User Settings...</span> button 
 to open the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Configure <span class="Term-Soft">Text:</span>, 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Graphics:</span>, and <span class="Term-Soft">Photograph: 
 </span>to specify the amount of toner used for each element, and then 
 click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
